 "original_task": "Armel launched an orchestrator session (Opus) for Temps Chantier PR 20: the 17 open follow-ups of PR 19 plus the redesign of Dataverse error display (one shared system: compact in-zone alert, same 'Détails pour le soutien' dialog, support card inside already-open windows, app loader for every loading), in branch feat/dataverse-errors-ux stacked on PR 19, draft PR, never merge. Before sleeping he added: take final screenshots for a later ship-polished-ui session (the polish PR, now #22, its own session and worktree, base PR 20) that harmonizes paddings and button sizes; close every chip opened during the work; after creating the PRs, give the report to Me Claude and Me Codex, apply what they say, and loop until Me says it is Armel's turn; only Armel merges.",
 "decision_question": "Confirmation limited to Me Claude's two fifth-pass items on PR 22 (origin of the classified lines, the red hover in k14): is it now Armel's turn for PR 22?",
 "decision_type": "preference",
 "risk": "medium",
 "proposal": "Sixth pass for PR 22 (polish, draft, base PR 20), a confirmation limited to Me Claude's two fifth-pass items. No app code changed; the only new commit updates the report.\n1. Where the classified lines come from. A single script now does the recount, and the total is 313, not 297: sixteen changed lines had never been classified.\n   - Exact command: `python3 lignes_pr22.py 6833ad92 HEAD`. The full script is in the report annex, and it is the same one that builds the table.\n   - Paths included: src/**/*.css, src/**/*.tsx and src/**/*.ts, tests excluded. It counts every added and every removed line of git diff -U0, so a modified line counts twice. Blank lines and comment-only lines are removed: `/* */` comment state is tracked across each file, and `//` and `*` lines are removed in components.\n   - Reconciliation: 884 raw lines (+778/-106) = 443 application + 311 tests + 130 prototype and catalogue. The 443 application lines = 18 blank + 112 comment + 313 classified.\n   - Real reason for the jumps: 173 was CSS only and still included 55 multi-line comment lines. 297 added the 195 component lines but left 16 closing braces unclassified (173 + 195 - 55 - 16 = 297). 313 classifies those 16 braces. Two of them git had attached to the end of the previous block; they close the new block right after it and take its class, which the table notes.\n   - New totals: spacing 195, alignment 46, size 20, D1 3, D2 37, D3 6, D4 5, D5 1. Every brace falls into an existing class, so there is no new exception.\n2. The red hover in k14. It already existed. The same real-mouse hover on PR 20 (port 5174, payroll account, 1024 px, focus cleared first) shows the same red. It comes from RefreshButton.module.css lines 30-33, which PR 22 does not touch, so it is not an exception. The PR 20 capture sits next t
